      { path: "SKILL.md", content: `---
name: nexus-tracing
description: Views and analyzes LLM execution traces, inspects individual generations (with full prompt/response data), tracks costs and token usage, runs analytics queries (summary, cost breakdown, timeline), exports trace data in JSON/CSV, and deletes traces via the Public API v1.
---

# Nexus LLM Tracing

View LLM execution traces; analyze cost + tokens; debug generation behavior. Setup/envelope → CLAUDE.md.

## CLI

\`\`\`bash
nexus tracing traces                            # list traces
nexus tracing trace <id>                        # get trace + generations
nexus tracing delete <id>                       # delete trace (hard)
nexus tracing generations                       # list generations across traces
nexus tracing generation <id>                   # get gen detail (prompt/response — only here)
nexus tracing models                            # list distinct models
nexus tracing summary                           # analytics summary (counts, cost, tokens)
nexus tracing cost-breakdown --group-by model   # cost by model/agent/workflow
nexus tracing timeline --granularity day        # time-series
nexus tracing export <id> --format csv          # single-trace export
nexus tracing export-bulk --format json         # bulk (max 1000)
\`\`\`

All commands accept \`--json\`. Dashboard: \`https://app.nexusgpt.io/settings/llm-tracing\`.

## Concepts

- **Trace** — groups multiple LLM calls (generations) in a single execution/session. Tracks total cost, tokens, duration.
- **Generation** — single LLM call. Records provider, model, system prompt, messages, tools, temperature, response, tokens, cost, timing. Prompt/response only in single-gen endpoint.
- **Analytics** — \`summary\` (counts/cost/tokens/avg duration + prev-period comparison) / \`cost-breakdown\` (by model/agent/workflow) / \`timeline\` (hour/day/week).

## Statuses

- Trace: \`IN_PROGRESS\`, \`COMPLETED\`, \`FAILED\`
- Generation: \`PENDING\`, \`RUNNING\`, \`COMPLETED\`, \`FAILED\`
- Providers: \`OPEN_AI\`, \`ANTHROPIC\`, \`GOOGLE_AI\`

## Token + Cost Fields — silent-failure traps

**Token counts (\`totalInputTokens\`, \`totalOutputTokens\`, \`inputTokens\`, \`outputTokens\`) returned as STRINGS** (BigInt internally). Parse w/ \`BigInt()\` or \`parseInt()\`.
✗ \`tokens + N\` w/o parseInt → string concatenation instead of math → silent corruption.
RIGHT: \`parseInt(tokens) + N\`.

**Cost fields:** \`totalCost\` on traces = USD float. \`costInUSDTenThousandths\` on generations = integer in 1/10000th USD; divide by 10000 for USD.

## Filtering

**Trace filters:** \`status\` (IN_PROGRESS/COMPLETED/FAILED), \`agentId\`/\`workflowId\`/\`chatId\` (uuid), \`model\` (string, max 255 chars, partial match), \`startDate\`/\`endDate\` (ISO 8601), \`sortBy\` (startedAt/totalCost/totalDurationMs), \`order\` (asc/desc).

**Generation filters:** \`traceId\`/\`agentId\`/\`aiTaskId\` (uuid), \`provider\` (OPEN_AI/ANTHROPIC/GOOGLE_AI), \`modelName\` (string partial), \`status\` (PENDING/RUNNING/COMPLETED/FAILED), \`startDate\`/\`endDate\` (ISO 8601), \`minCost\`/\`maxCost\` (number USD).

## Latency-isolation pattern (per R#5)

Slow workflow? Re-run plugin action w/ \`nexus external-tool execute\` standalone, compare \`executionTimeMs\`-equivalent against trace's gen duration. Isolated fast + in-workflow slow → overhead in wiring, not the tool. Full → \`nexus-tool-execute/TOOL_EXECUTION_GUIDE.md\`.

## Error Handling

| HTTP | When |
|---|---|
| 400 | Invalid query params or body |
| 404 | Trace or generation ID doesn't exist |
| 403 | Missing \`tracing:read\` or \`tracing:write\` scope |

## Data Retention

Traces auto-expire (default 7 days, min 7 days). Not configurable via public API.` },
      { path: "examples/01-list-and-inspect-traces.ts", content: `#!/usr/bin/env npx tsx
/**
 * List and Inspect Traces
 *
 * Demonstrates: listing traces with filters, getting trace details,
 * inspecting nested generations.
 *
 * Run: NEXUS_API_KEY=nxs_... npx tsx examples/01-list-and-inspect-traces.ts
 */

import { createClient } from "../../shared/api-client";
import { assert, assertDefined, log, success } from "../../shared/helpers";

async function main() {
  const api = createClient();

  // ═══ STEP 1: List recent traces ═══
  log("list", "Listing recent traces...");
  const { data: traces } = await api.get("/tracing/traces", {
    limit: 5,
    order: "desc",
    sortBy: "startedAt"
  });
  assert(Array.isArray(traces), "traces is array");
  log("list", \`Found \${traces.length} traces\`);

  if (traces.length === 0) {
    log("skip", "No traces found — run a workflow or chat to generate traces.");
    return;
  }

  // ═══ STEP 2: Get trace detail ═══
  const traceId = traces[0].id;
  log("get", \`Getting trace \${traceId}...\`);
  const { data: trace } = await api.get(\`/tracing/traces/\${traceId}\`);
  assertDefined(trace.id, "trace.id");
  assertDefined(trace.status, "trace.status");
  log("get", \`Trace status: \${trace.status}, generations: \${trace.generations?.length ?? 0}\`);

  // ═══ STEP 3: Inspect a generation ═══
  if (trace.generations && trace.generations.length > 0) {
    const genId = trace.generations[0].id;
    log("get", \`Getting generation \${genId}...\`);
    const { data: gen } = await api.get(\`/tracing/generations/\${genId}\`);
    assertDefined(gen.provider, "gen.provider");
    assertDefined(gen.modelName, "gen.modelName");
    log("get", \`Provider: \${gen.provider}, Model: \${gen.modelName}\`);
    log("get", \`Prompt length: \${gen.systemPrompt?.length ?? 0} chars\`);
    log("get", \`Response length: \${gen.response?.length ?? 0} chars\`);
  }

  // ═══ STEP 4: Filter by status ═══
  log("filter", "Listing failed traces...");
  const { data: failed } = await api.get("/tracing/traces", { status: "FAILED", limit: 3 });
  log("filter", \`Found \${failed.length} failed traces\`);

  // ═══ STEP 5: List distinct models ═══
  log("models", "Listing distinct models...");
  const { data: models } = await api.get("/tracing/models");
  log("models", \`Models used: \${models.join(", ") || "none"}\`);

  success("Trace inspection complete!");
}

main().catch((err) => {
  console.error("\\nFailed:", err.message);
  process.exit(1);
});` },
      { path: "examples/02-debug-failed-generations.ts", content: `#!/usr/bin/env npx tsx
/**
 * Debug Failed Generations
 *
 * Demonstrates: querying generations across traces to find failures,
 * inspecting error messages and request details.
 *
 * Run: NEXUS_API_KEY=nxs_... npx tsx examples/02-debug-failed-generations.ts
 */

import { createClient } from "../../shared/api-client";
import { assert, log, success } from "../../shared/helpers";

async function main() {
  const api = createClient();

  // ═══ STEP 1: Find all failed generations ═══
  log("search", "Searching for failed generations...");
  const { data: failedGens } = await api.get("/tracing/generations", {
    status: "FAILED",
    limit: 10,
    order: "desc"
  });
  assert(Array.isArray(failedGens), "failedGens is array");
  log("search", \`Found \${failedGens.length} failed generations\`);

  if (failedGens.length === 0) {
    log("skip", "No failed generations found.");
    return;
  }

  // ═══ STEP 2: Inspect each failure ═══
  for (const gen of failedGens.slice(0, 3)) {
    log("inspect", \`\\nGeneration \${gen.id}:\`);
    log("inspect", \`  Model: \${gen.provider}/\${gen.modelName}\`);
    log("inspect", \`  Error: \${gen.errorMessage || "no error message"}\`);
    log("inspect", \`  AI Task: \${gen.aiTaskName || "n/a"}\`);
    log("inspect", \`  Duration: \${gen.durationMs ?? "n/a"}ms\`);

    // Get full details including the prompt that caused the error
    const { data: detail } = await api.get(\`/tracing/generations/\${gen.id}\`);
    log("inspect", \`  System prompt: \${(detail.systemPrompt || "").substring(0, 100)}...\`);
    log("inspect", \`  Messages: \${JSON.stringify(detail.messages || []).substring(0, 200)}...\`);
    log("inspect", \`  Temperature: \${detail.temperature ?? "default"}\`);
  }

  // ═══ STEP 3: Filter by provider ═══
  log("filter", "\\nFailed Anthropic generations specifically:");
  const { data: anthropicFails } = await api.get("/tracing/generations", {
    status: "FAILED",
    provider: "ANTHROPIC",
    limit: 5
  });
  log("filter", \`Found \${anthropicFails.length} failed Anthropic generations\`);

  success("Failure debugging complete!");
}

main().catch((err) => {
  console.error("\\nFailed:", err.message);
  process.exit(1);
});` },
      { path: "examples/03-analytics-dashboard.ts", content: `#!/usr/bin/env npx tsx
/**
 * Analytics Dashboard
 *
 * Demonstrates: summary stats, cost breakdown, and timeline data
 * for building an LLM usage dashboard.
 *
 * Run: NEXUS_API_KEY=nxs_... npx tsx examples/03-analytics-dashboard.ts
 */

import { createClient } from "../../shared/api-client";
import { log, success } from "../../shared/helpers";

async function main() {
  const api = createClient();

  const startDate = new Date(Date.now() - 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();
  const endDate = new Date().toISOString();

  // ═══ STEP 1: Get summary stats ═══
  log("summary", "Fetching analytics summary...");
  const { data: summary } = await api.get("/tracing/analytics/summary", { startDate, endDate });

  log("summary", \`Total traces: \${summary.totalTraces}\`);
  log("summary", \`  Completed: \${summary.completedTraces}\`);
  log("summary", \`  Failed: \${summary.failedTraces}\`);
  log("summary", \`  In progress: \${summary.inProgressTraces}\`);
  log("summary", \`Total cost: $\${summary.totalCost?.toFixed(4) ?? "0"}\`);
  log("summary", \`Input tokens: \${summary.totalInputTokens}\`);
  log("summary", \`Output tokens: \${summary.totalOutputTokens}\`);
  log("summary", \`Avg duration: \${summary.avgDurationMs?.toFixed(0) ?? "n/a"}ms\`);
  log("summary", \`Distinct models: \${summary.distinctModelCount}\`);

  if (summary.previousPeriod) {
    const pct = (curr: number, prev: number) =>
      prev > 0 ? \`\${(((curr - prev) / prev) * 100).toFixed(1)}%\` : "n/a";
    log("compare", \`Cost change: \${pct(summary.totalCost, summary.previousPeriod.totalCost)}\`);
    log(
      "compare",
      \`Trace count change: \${pct(summary.totalTraces, summary.previousPeriod.totalTraces)}\`
    );
  }

  // ═══ STEP 2: Cost breakdown by model ═══
  log("breakdown", "\\nCost breakdown by model:");
  const { data: byModel } = await api.get("/tracing/analytics/cost-breakdown", {
    startDate,
    endDate,
    groupBy: "model"
  });
  for (const entry of byModel.entries ?? []) {
    log(
      "breakdown",
      \`  \${entry.groupLabel}: $\${entry.totalCost.toFixed(4)} (\${entry.generationCount} gens)\`
    );
  }

  // ═══ STEP 3: Cost breakdown by agent ═══
  log("breakdown", "\\nCost breakdown by agent:");
  const { data: byAgent } = await api.get("/tracing/analytics/cost-breakdown", {
    startDate,
    endDate,
    groupBy: "agent"
  });
  for (const entry of byAgent.entries ?? []) {
    log("breakdown", \`  \${entry.groupLabel || entry.groupKey}: $\${entry.totalCost.toFixed(4)}\`);
  }

  // ═══ STEP 4: Timeline (daily) ═══
  log("timeline", "\\nDaily timeline:");
  const { data: timeline } = await api.get("/tracing/analytics/timeline", {
    startDate,
    endDate,
    granularity: "day"
  });
  for (const point of timeline.points ?? []) {
    const date = new Date(point.date).toLocaleDateString();
    log("timeline", \`  \${date}: \${point.traceCount} traces, $\${point.totalCost.toFixed(4)}\`);
  }

  success("Analytics dashboard complete!");
}

main().catch((err) => {
  console.error("\\nFailed:", err.message);
  process.exit(1);
});` },
      { path: "examples/04-cost-analysis.ts", content: `#!/usr/bin/env npx tsx
/**
 * Cost Analysis
 *
 * Demonstrates: finding expensive traces, analyzing cost patterns,
 * comparing cost across models and workflows.
 *
 * Run: NEXUS_API_KEY=nxs_... npx tsx examples/04-cost-analysis.ts
 */

import { createClient } from "../../shared/api-client";
import { log, success } from "../../shared/helpers";

async function main() {
  const api = createClient();

  // ═══ STEP 1: Find most expensive traces ═══
  log("cost", "Finding most expensive traces...");
  const { data: expensive } = await api.get("/tracing/traces", {
    sortBy: "totalCost",
    order: "desc",
    limit: 5,
    status: "COMPLETED"
  });

  for (const trace of expensive) {
    const cost = trace.totalCost != null ? \`$\${trace.totalCost.toFixed(4)}\` : "n/a";
    const tokens =
      parseInt(trace.totalInputTokens || "0") + parseInt(trace.totalOutputTokens || "0");
    log("cost", \`  \${trace.id}: \${cost} (\${tokens} tokens, \${trace.generationCount} gens)\`);
  }

  // ═══ STEP 2: Find expensive generations ═══
  log("cost", "\\nMost expensive individual LLM calls:");
  const { data: expensiveGens } = await api.get("/tracing/generations", {
    sortBy: "costInUSDTenThousandths",
    order: "desc",
    limit: 5,
    status: "COMPLETED"
  });

  for (const gen of expensiveGens) {
    const cost =
      gen.costInUSDTenThousandths != null
        ? \`$\${(gen.costInUSDTenThousandths / 10000).toFixed(6)}\`
        : "n/a";
    log("cost", \`  \${gen.modelName}: \${cost} (in: \${gen.inputTokens}, out: \${gen.outputTokens})\`);
  }

  // ═══ STEP 3: Compare model costs ═══
  log("compare", "\\nCost by model:");
  const { data: byModel } = await api.get("/tracing/analytics/cost-breakdown", {
    groupBy: "model"
  });

  const totalCost = byModel.entries.reduce((sum: number, e: any) => sum + e.totalCost, 0);
  for (const entry of byModel.entries) {
    const pct = totalCost > 0 ? ((entry.totalCost / totalCost) * 100).toFixed(1) : "0";
    log("compare", \`  \${entry.groupLabel}: $\${entry.totalCost.toFixed(4)} (\${pct}% of total)\`);
  }

  // ═══ STEP 4: Compare workflow costs ═══
  log("compare", "\\nCost by workflow:");
  const { data: byWorkflow } = await api.get("/tracing/analytics/cost-breakdown", {
    groupBy: "workflow"
  });

  for (const entry of byWorkflow.entries) {
    const avgPerTrace = entry.traceCount > 0 ? entry.totalCost / entry.traceCount : 0;
    log(
      "compare",
      \`  \${entry.groupLabel || "unnamed"}: $\${entry.totalCost.toFixed(4)} total, $\${avgPerTrace.toFixed(4)}/trace\`
    );
  }

  success("Cost analysis complete!");
}

main().catch((err) => {
  console.error("\\nFailed:", err.message);
  process.exit(1);
});` },
      { path: "examples/05-export-traces.ts", content: `#!/usr/bin/env npx tsx
/**
 * Export Traces
 *
 * Demonstrates: exporting single traces and bulk exports
 * in JSON and CSV formats.
 *
 * Run: NEXUS_API_KEY=nxs_... npx tsx examples/05-export-traces.ts
 */

import { createClient } from "../../shared/api-client";
import { assert, assertDefined, log, success } from "../../shared/helpers";

async function main() {
  const api = createClient();

  // ═══ STEP 1: Find a trace to export ═══
  log("list", "Finding a trace to export...");
  const { data: traces } = await api.get("/tracing/traces", { limit: 1 });

  if (traces.length === 0) {
    log("skip", "No traces found. Run a workflow or chat first.");
    return;
  }

  const traceId = traces[0].id;

  // ═══ STEP 2: Export as JSON ═══
  log("export", \`Exporting trace \${traceId} as JSON...\`);
  const { data: jsonExport } = await api.post(\`/tracing/traces/\${traceId}/export\`, {
    format: "json"
  });
  assertDefined(jsonExport.content, "jsonExport.content");
  assert(jsonExport.contentType === "application/json", "is JSON");
  assert(jsonExport.filename.endsWith(".json"), "filename ends with .json");
  log("export", \`JSON export: \${jsonExport.content.length} chars, file: \${jsonExport.filename}\`);

  // ═══ STEP 3: Export as CSV ═══
  log("export", \`Exporting trace \${traceId} as CSV...\`);
  const { data: csvExport } = await api.post(\`/tracing/traces/\${traceId}/export\`, {
    format: "csv"
  });
  assertDefined(csvExport.content, "csvExport.content");
  assert(csvExport.contentType === "text/csv", "is CSV");
  const csvLines = csvExport.content.split("\\n");
  log("export", \`CSV export: \${csvLines.length} rows (including header)\`);
  log("export", \`Headers: \${csvLines[0]}\`);

  // ═══ STEP 4: Bulk export ═══
  log("bulk", "Bulk exporting completed traces...");
  const { data: bulkExport } = await api.post("/tracing/export", {
    format: "json",
    status: "COMPLETED",
    limit: 10
  });
  assertDefined(bulkExport.content, "bulkExport.content");
  const parsed = JSON.parse(bulkExport.content);
  log("bulk", \`Exported \${parsed.length} traces, file: \${bulkExport.filename}\`);

  // ═══ STEP 5: Bulk export as CSV ═══
  log("bulk", "Bulk exporting as CSV...");
  const { data: bulkCsv } = await api.post("/tracing/export", {
    format: "csv",
    limit: 10
  });
  const bulkCsvLines = bulkCsv.content.split("\\n");
  log("bulk", \`CSV bulk export: \${bulkCsvLines.length} rows\`);

  success("Export complete!");
}

main().catch((err) => {
  console.error("\\nFailed:", err.message);
  process.exit(1);
});` },
      { path: "reference/analytics.md", content: `# Tracing Analytics Reference

## Summary Endpoint

\`\`\`bash
nexus tracing analytics summary [--start-date ...] [--end-date ...] --json
\`\`\`

Returns aggregate statistics for the organization's LLM usage. When \`--start-date\` and \`--end-date\` are provided, also returns a \`previousPeriod\` comparison (same duration, shifted back).

### Response Structure

\`\`\`json
{
  "totalTraces": 150,
  "completedTraces": 120,
  "failedTraces": 10,
  "inProgressTraces": 20,
  "totalCost": 12.5432,
  "totalInputTokens": "4500000",
  "totalOutputTokens": "1200000",
  "avgDurationMs": 2340.5,
  "distinctModelCount": 4,
  "previousPeriod": {
    "totalTraces": 130,
    "totalCost": 10.21,
    "totalInputTokens": "3800000",
    "totalOutputTokens": "1000000"
  }
}
\`\`\`

### Computing Deltas

\`\`\`typescript
const pctChange = (current, previous) =>
  previous > 0 ? ((current - previous) / previous) * 100 : 0;

const costChange = pctChange(summary.totalCost, summary.previousPeriod.totalCost);
// e.g., +22.9%
\`\`\`

## Cost Breakdown Endpoint

\`\`\`bash
nexus tracing analytics cost-breakdown [--group-by model|agent|workflow] [--start-date ...] [--end-date ...] --json
\`\`\`

Groups cost data by \`model\`, \`agent\`, or \`workflow\`.

### groupBy=model

Groups by \`modelName\` on generations. \`groupKey\` and \`groupLabel\` are both the model name string.

### groupBy=agent

Groups by \`agentId\` on traces. \`groupKey\` is the agent UUID, \`groupLabel\` is the agent's display name.

### groupBy=workflow

Groups by \`workflowId\` on traces. \`groupKey\` is the workflow UUID, \`groupLabel\` is the workflow name.

### Notes

- Entries are sorted by \`totalCost\` descending
- \`totalCost\` is in USD (already converted from tenThousandths)
- Only traces/generations with non-null agent/workflow IDs are included in agent/workflow breakdowns

## Timeline Endpoint

\`\`\`bash
nexus tracing analytics timeline [--granularity hour|day|week] [--start-date ...] [--end-date ...] --json
\`\`\`

Time-series data grouped by granularity.

### Granularity Options

| Value  | Bucket size | Best for         |
| ------ | ----------- | ---------------- |
| \`hour\` | 1 hour      | Last 24-48 hours |
| \`day\`  | 1 day       | Last 7-30 days   |
| \`week\` | 1 week      | Last 90+ days    |

### Response

Points are sorted chronologically (ascending). Each point represents one time bucket. The \`date\` field is the start of the bucket in ISO 8601 format.

### Notes

- Points with zero activity are omitted (no zero-fill)
- The \`totalCost\` in timeline points may double-count if a trace has multiple generations (cost is summed from traces, not generations)
- \`avgDurationMs\` is the average trace duration for traces that started in that bucket` },
      { path: "reference/endpoints.md", content: `# Tracing API Endpoints

## Traces

### List Traces

\`\`\`
GET /public/v1/tracing/traces
\`\`\`

Query: \`page\`, \`limit\`, \`status\`, \`agentId\`, \`workflowId\`, \`chatId\`, \`model\`, \`startDate\`, \`endDate\`, \`sortBy\`, \`order\`
Returns: \`{ success, data: TraceSummary[], meta: { total, page, limit, totalPages, hasMore } }\`

### Get Trace Detail

\`\`\`
GET /public/v1/tracing/traces/:traceId
\`\`\`

Returns: \`{ success, data: TraceDetail }\` (includes nested generation summaries)

### Delete Trace

\`\`\`
DELETE /public/v1/tracing/traces/:traceId
\`\`\`

Returns: \`{ success, data: { id } }\`

## Generations

### List Generations

\`\`\`
GET /public/v1/tracing/generations
\`\`\`

Query: \`page\`, \`limit\`, \`traceId\`, \`provider\`, \`modelName\`, \`status\`, \`agentId\`, \`aiTaskId\`, \`startDate\`, \`endDate\`, \`minCost\`, \`maxCost\`, \`sortBy\`, \`order\`
Returns: \`{ success, data: GenerationSummary[], meta }\`

### Get Generation Detail

\`\`\`
GET /public/v1/tracing/generations/:generationId
\`\`\`

Returns: \`{ success, data: GenerationDetail }\` (includes systemPrompt, messages, tools, response)

## Models

### List Distinct Models

\`\`\`
GET /public/v1/tracing/models
\`\`\`

Returns: \`{ success, data: string[] }\`

## Analytics

### Summary

\`\`\`
GET /public/v1/tracing/analytics/summary
\`\`\`

Query: \`startDate\`, \`endDate\`
Returns: \`{ success, data: TracingSummary }\`

TracingSummary fields:

- \`totalTraces\`, \`completedTraces\`, \`failedTraces\`, \`inProgressTraces\`
- \`totalCost\` (USD), \`totalInputTokens\`, \`totalOutputTokens\` (strings)
- \`avgDurationMs\`, \`distinctModelCount\`
- \`previousPeriod\` (same fields, null if no date range given)

### Cost Breakdown

\`\`\`
GET /public/v1/tracing/analytics/cost-breakdown
\`\`\`

Query: \`startDate\`, \`endDate\`, \`groupBy\` (model | agent | workflow)
Returns: \`{ success, data: { entries: CostBreakdownEntry[] } }\`

CostBreakdownEntry fields:

- \`groupKey\`, \`groupLabel\`
- \`totalCost\` (USD), \`totalInputTokens\`, \`totalOutputTokens\`
- \`traceCount\`, \`generationCount\`

### Timeline

\`\`\`
GET /public/v1/tracing/analytics/timeline
\`\`\`

Query: \`startDate\`, \`endDate\`, \`granularity\` (hour | day | week)
Returns: \`{ success, data: { points: TimelinePoint[] } }\`

TimelinePoint fields:

- \`date\` (ISO string)
- \`traceCount\`, \`generationCount\`
- \`totalCost\`, \`totalInputTokens\`, \`totalOutputTokens\`
- \`avgDurationMs\`

## Export

### Export Single Trace

\`\`\`
POST /public/v1/tracing/traces/:traceId/export
\`\`\`

Body: \`{ format: "json" | "csv" }\`
Returns: \`{ success, data: { content, contentType, filename } }\`

### Bulk Export

\`\`\`
POST /public/v1/tracing/export
\`\`\`

Body: \`{ format, status?, agentId?, workflowId?, startDate?, endDate?, limit? }\`
Limit max: 1000, default: 100
Returns: \`{ success, data: { content, contentType, filename } }\`

## SDK Usage

\`\`\`typescript
import { NexusClient } from "@agent-nexus/sdk";
const client = new NexusClient({ apiKey: "nxs_..." });

// Traces
const { data: traces, meta } = await client.tracing.listTraces({ status: "FAILED" });
const trace = await client.tracing.getTrace(traceId);
await client.tracing.deleteTrace(traceId);

// Generations
const { data: gens } = await client.tracing.listGenerations({ provider: "ANTHROPIC" });
const gen = await client.tracing.getGeneration(generationId);

// Models
const models = await client.tracing.listModels();

// Analytics
const summary = await client.tracing.getSummary({ startDate: "2026-03-01" });
const breakdown = await client.tracing.getCostBreakdown({ groupBy: "model" });
const timeline = await client.tracing.getTimeline({ granularity: "day" });

// Export
const exported = await client.tracing.exportTrace(traceId, { format: "csv" });
const bulk = await client.tracing.bulkExport({ format: "json", limit: 50 });
\`\`\`` },
      { path: "reference/export.md", content: `# Export Reference

## Formats

### JSON Export

Single trace export returns the full \`TraceDetail\` object (including all generation summaries) serialized as pretty-printed JSON.

Bulk export returns an array of \`TraceDetail\` objects.

### CSV Export

CSV format has one row per generation. Traces with no generations get a single row with empty generation columns.

**Columns:**

\`\`\`
traceId, traceStatus, agentId, workflowId, generationId, provider, modelName,
generationStatus, inputTokens, outputTokens, costUSD, durationMs, aiTaskId,
aiTaskName, nodeId, errorMessage, startedAt, completedAt
\`\`\`

- \`costUSD\` is calculated as \`costInUSDTenThousandths / 10000\` with 6 decimal places
- All date fields are ISO 8601 strings
- CSV fields containing commas, quotes, or newlines are properly escaped
- Fields starting with \`=\`, \`+\`, \`-\`, \`@\`, \`|\` are prefixed with \`'\` to prevent formula injection

## Single Trace Export

\`\`\`bash
nexus tracing export <traceId> [--format json|csv]
\`\`\`

Response:

\`\`\`json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "content": "...", // The export content as a string
    "contentType": "application/json", // or "text/csv"
    "filename": "trace-{id}.json" // or .csv
  }
}
\`\`\`

## Bulk Export

\`\`\`bash
nexus tracing export-bulk [--format json|csv] [--status COMPLETED] [--agent-id ...] [--workflow-id ...] [--start-date 2026-03-01] [--end-date 2026-03-30] [--limit 100]
\`\`\`

Response: Same structure as single export, with filename like \`traces-export-2026-03-30T12-00-00-000Z.json\`.

## CLI Export

\`\`\`bash
# Export single trace as JSON to stdout
nexus tracing export <id>

# Export as CSV and redirect to file
nexus tracing export <id> --format csv > trace.csv

# Bulk export failed traces
nexus tracing export-bulk --status FAILED --format csv > failed-traces.csv

# Bulk export with filters
nexus tracing export-bulk --agent-id abc --start-date 2026-03-01 --limit 500
\`\`\`

## SDK Export

\`\`\`typescript
// Single trace
const { content, contentType, filename } = await client.tracing.exportTrace(traceId, {
  format: "csv"
});
fs.writeFileSync(filename, content);

// Bulk
const bulk = await client.tracing.bulkExport({
  format: "json",
  status: "FAILED",
  limit: 200
});
fs.writeFileSync(bulk.filename, bulk.content);
\`\`\`` }
